    <string name="meals_method_title">How meals are estimated</string>
    <string name="meals_method_body">Only food that was actually collected counts.\n\n• 1 portion = 1 meal.\n• Kilograms are divided by %1$d g per meal, the conversion factor WRAP (UK) uses for redistributed surplus food. Results are rounded down.\n• Pieces, boxes, packs and litres have no known weight, so they are not converted rather than guessed.\n\nThis is an estimate of meals, not a measurement. ShareBite does not calculate carbon or money saved.</string>

